{# Buyer / auction information pack (SPEC 12 step 6c), built to the Info Pack
   Playbook (docs/INFO-PACK-PLAYBOOK.md).

   A PAGINATED A4 DOCUMENT, not a web page: every section is a real 210x297mm
   `.page` block with 18mm padding and `page-break-after`, so the printed PDF
   (engine/render/rasterize.py html_to_pdf) breaks exactly where the design
   intends rather than wherever the text happens to reflow. `@page { margin: 0 }`
   makes the ivory paper run to the sheet edge; `print-color-adjust: exact` keeps
   the colour.

   Page order (playbook 4, adapted to an auto-generated per-property pack):
     1. Cover
     2. Property information            (MUST be page 2)
     2b. Schedule of portions           (only a multi portion property, and only
                                         when the schedule cannot share page 2)
     2c. Conditions of sale             (only when they cannot share page 2)
     3. Photographs                     (only when the record carries photos)
     4. Accommodation and features      (the residential stand-in for the
                                         playbook's loose-asset register; MUST
                                         come before the highlights)
     5. Investment highlights           (MUST be second last, Highlight | Detail)
     6. Contact and disclaimers         (MUST be last)
   Pages 2b, 2c, 3, 4 and 5 render only when this property actually holds that
   data: an empty stub page is worse than no page. The order rule then applies
   to the pages that do render.

   PAGE COMPOSITION IS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED. Every block on a sheet has a cost
   in tenths of a millimetre, taken off the printed page (the constants below),
   and the template adds those costs up to decide what shares a sheet and what
   moves to its own. Three rules follow from it:
     - a long list is split so every page carries the same PROPORTION of its own
       budget, never filled to the brim page by page, which is what leaves a
       last page holding two orphan rows;
     - a list that is short for its page has its row padding opened up to fill
       the sheet (`padmm`), so a light page reads as designed spacing rather
       than as a heading with nothing under it;
     - what is STILL empty after that, once a list has taken all the padding it
       can carry, is measured (`FILL_MIN`) and given a photograph band that
       flexes to the exact height left over. No sheet in the pack carries a hand
       sized hole between its content and its footnote.

   Rendered from `public_view` only, so owner name/ID, occupant contact, bond and
   arrears are structurally absent (SPEC 4.4). No valuation figure appears
   anywhere: the municipal and professional valuations are stripped from the
   projection on purpose (owner directive, D32), so the money element is always
   the offers framing or the auction line.

   Auction vs sale is the key branch (playbook 5): the pack only uses auction /
   bidding language when sale_process.method == "auction". A normal listing is a
   "Buyer information pack" using offer language ("How to proceed", "Submit a
   written offer", "conditions of sale"), never auction / bid words. Figures are
   hedged (approx.), there are no em or en dashes, and both disclaimers appear
   verbatim (playbook 8). The pack is issued as Dynamic Auctioneers whichever
   way the property is sold, so the lockup is pinned to the auctioneers brand:
   the running head, the contact block and the legal entity all say Dynamic
   Auctioneers and the logo must not say something else. #}
{% import "_adparts.html.j2" as parts %}

{% set is_auction = (vm.method == 'auction') %}
{% set pack_label = 'Auction information pack' if is_auction else 'Buyer information pack' %}

{# --- the auction line: channel, date, time, from record fields only ------ #}
{% set abits = [] %}
{% if vm.auction_channel %}{% set _ = abits.append(vm.auction_channel) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.auction_date %}{% set _ = abits.append(vm.auction_date) %}{% endif %}
{% set auction_line %}
{%- if abits %}{{ abits | join(', ') }}{% if vm.auction_time %} at {{ vm.auction_time }}{% endif %}{% else %}Date to be confirmed{% endif -%}
{% endset %}
{% set offer_headline = (vm.price_display or 'Offers invited') %}

{# --- the extent, in the words the document uses everywhere --------------- #}
{% set extent_str %}
{%- if vm.size_display %}approx. {{ vm.size_display }} m2{% if vm.size_ha %}, about {{ vm.size_ha }} ha{% endif %}{% endif -%}
{% endset %}

{# --- stat cells (up to 4), each one a fact the record actually holds ----- #}
{% set stats = [] %}
{% if vm.size_display %}{% set _ = stats.append(((vm.size_ha ~ ' ha') if vm.size_ha else (vm.size_display ~ ' m2'), 'Approx. extent')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.beds %}{% set _ = stats.append((vm.beds, 'Bedroom' if vm.beds == '1' else 'Bedrooms')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.baths %}{% set _ = stats.append((vm.baths, 'Bathroom' if vm.baths == '1' else 'Bathrooms')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.garages and vm.garages != '0' %}{% set _ = stats.append((vm.garages, 'Garage' if vm.garages == '1' else 'Garages')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.flatlet_present %}{% set _ = stats.append((vm.flatlet_beds or 'Yes', 'Bed flatlet' if vm.flatlet_beds else 'Flatlet')) %}{% endif %}
{% set stats = stats[:4] %}

{# --- accommodation phrase, reused on the highlights table ---------------- #}
{% set accom = [] %}
{% if vm.beds %}{% set _ = accom.append(vm.beds ~ (' bedroom' if vm.beds == '1' else ' bedrooms')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.baths %}{% set _ = accom.append(vm.baths ~ (' bathroom' if vm.baths == '1' else ' bathrooms')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.separate_toilet %}{% set _ = accom.append('separate toilet') %}{% endif %}

{% set flatlet_line %}
{%- if vm.flatlet_beds %}{{ vm.flatlet_beds }} bedroom flatlet{% else %}Separate flatlet{% endif %}
{%- if vm.flatlet_features %} with {{ vm.flatlet_features | join(', ') | lower }}{% endif -%}
{% endset %}

{# The hero is already on the cover, so the gallery page carries the next six. #}
{% set shots = (vm.photos or [])[1:7] %}

{# Photographs that neither the cover nor the gallery page used feed the bands
   that fill short pages. When they run out the band cycles back through the
   set: a photograph the buyer has already seen reads better than a third of an
   empty sheet, which is the whole point of the band. #}
{% set fill_photos = vm.photos or [] %}
{% set pool = namespace(i=(shots | length) + 1) %}

{# =========================================================================
   SHEET GEOMETRY. All costs are tenths of a millimetre, measured off the
   printed A4 (rasterise the PDF and read the block positions; the numbers
   below are within a millimetre of the real thing).
   ========================================================================= #}
{# Body region of an ordinary sheet: from 56mm (under the section rule) to
   255mm (above a three line footnote). The features page footnote runs to one
   line, so that page has ~8mm more. #}
{% set REGION = 1990 %}
{% set REGION_WIDE = 2075 %}
{% set H3 = 61 %}          {# a small caps sub head plus its margin #}
{% set GAP = 70 %}         {# the 7mm gap between two blocks #}
{% set LINE = 49 %}        {# one line of 11.5px body text #}
{% set ROW_PAD = 25 %}     {# default vertical padding on a list row, per side #}
{% set SCHED_PAD = 26 %}   {# ... on a schedule row #}
{% set KV_PAD = 23 %}      {# ... on a card row #}
{% set CARD_CHROME = 161 %}{# card padding top and bottom plus its sub head #}
{# Characters per line, measured off the printed text (a full width list row is
   168mm at about 1.5mm a character). Rounded DOWN, so a wrap is counted a
   little early rather than a line late. #}
{% set CARD_CHARS = 28 %}  {# a card's value column, 43mm #}
{% set TERM_CHARS = 105 %} {# a full width list row, 168mm #}
{% set COL_CHARS = 48 %}   {# one of two feature columns, 77mm #}
{% set TH_ROW = 65 %}      {# a table's column heading row (schedule, highlights) #}
{% set OFFER_BOX = 305 %}  {# the gold "how it is offered" panel #}
{% set STAT_STRIP = 283 %} {# the four stat cells #}
{% set FLATLET_BOX = 345 %}{# the flatlet callout plus the gap above it #}
{% set SROW = LINE + 2 * SCHED_PAD %}
{% set SCHED_CHARS = 34 %} {# characters per line in the schedule's widest column #}

{# What counts as a hole. A sheet still holding this much empty height after its
   list has taken all the row padding it is allowed reads as a page that ran out
   of content, so it takes a photograph band. Under it the gap is small enough
   to read as designed spacing and is left alone. #}
{% set FILL_MIN = 300 %}   {# 30mm #}
{% set FILL_WIDE = 720 %}  {# from 72mm one photograph looks stretched: use two #}

{# Row padding that makes a list fill its share of the sheet: the space left
   over is divided over the rows instead of being left as a hole at the foot.
   Capped, because no amount of padding turns two bullet points into a page.
   `padraw` is the number (tenths of a millimetre) so the page can also work out
   what is STILL empty once the rows have taken their share; `padmm` is the same
   number as a CSS length. One formula, two readers. #}
{% macro padraw(budget, lines, rows, cap, base=ROW_PAD) %}{{ ([[(((budget - lines * LINE) // (2 * rows)) if rows else base), cap] | min, base] | max) }}{% endmacro %}

{% macro padmm(budget, lines, rows, cap, base=ROW_PAD) -%}
{{ (padraw(budget, lines, rows, cap, base) | int) / 10 }}mm
{%- endmacro %}

{# The band itself: one or two photographs that flex to whatever height the page
   has left. The height is CSS, not arithmetic, so a costing that is a few
   millimetres out still produces a sheet with no hole in it. #}
{% macro fill_band(wide=false) -%}
{%- if fill_photos -%}
{%- set n = 2 if (wide and (fill_photos | length) > 1) else 1 -%}
  <div class="band" style="grid-template-columns: repeat({{ n }}, 1fr)">
    {%- for k in range(n) %}
    <img src="{{ fill_photos[(pool.i + k) % (fill_photos | length)] }}" alt="Property photograph">
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
{%- set pool.i = pool.i + n -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# --- page 2's two cards, built as data so their height can be costed ----- #}
{# Title, not owner: the deeds identity of the property. The owner's name and
   ID are POPIA internal layer and are not in this projection (SPEC 4.4). #}
{% set title_rows = [] %}
{% if vm.title_type_label %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Title type', vm.title_type_label)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.scheme %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Scheme', vm.scheme ~ (', unit ' ~ vm.unit if vm.unit else ''))) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.erf %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Erf', vm.erf)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.legal_description %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Legal description', vm.legal_description)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.title_deed_no %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Title deed no.', vm.title_deed_no)) %}{% endif %}
{% if extent_str | trim %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Extent', extent_str | trim)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.zoning %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Zoning', vm.zoning)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.municipality %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Municipality', vm.municipality)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.province %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Province', vm.province)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.gps_str %}{% set _ = title_rows.append(('Coordinates', 'approx. ' ~ vm.gps_str)) %}{% endif %}

{% set offer_rows = [('Method of sale', 'Auction' if is_auction else 'Offers invited')] %}
{% if is_auction %}
{% if vm.auction_type %}{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Auction type', vm.auction_type ~ ' auction')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.auction_channel %}{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Held', vm.auction_channel)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.auction_date %}{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Auction date', vm.auction_date ~ (' at ' ~ vm.auction_time if vm.auction_time else ''))) %}{% endif %}
{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Confirmation', "The highest bid is subject to the seller's confirmation")) %}
{% else %}
{# Only a real asking figure earns a row of its own: repeating "Offers invited"
   under "Method of sale" says nothing twice. #}
{% if vm.price_display and vm.price_display | lower != 'offers invited' %}
{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Asking', vm.price_display)) %}
{% endif %}
{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Offers', 'In writing to Dynamic Auctioneers')) %}
{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Confirmation', "Any sale is subject to the seller's confirmation")) %}
{% endif %}
{% if vm.address %}{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Address', vm.address)) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.public_ref %}{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Reference', vm.public_ref)) %}{% endif %}
{% set _ = offer_rows.append(('Viewing', 'Strictly by appointment' if vm.viewing_by_appt else 'By arrangement with Dynamic Auctioneers')) %}

{% set tcost = namespace(n=0, lines=0) %}
{% for label, value in title_rows %}
{% set l = 1 + (((value | string | length) - 1) // CARD_CHARS) %}
{% set tcost.n = tcost.n + KV_PAD * 2 + LINE * l %}
{% set tcost.lines = tcost.lines + l %}
{% endfor %}
{% set ocost = namespace(n=0, lines=0) %}
{% for label, value in offer_rows %}
{% set l = 1 + (((value | string | length) - 1) // CARD_CHARS) %}
{% set ocost.n = ocost.n + KV_PAD * 2 + LINE * l %}
{% set ocost.lines = ocost.lines + l %}
{% endfor %}
{# The two cards sit side by side, so the block is as tall as the taller card. #}
{% set cards_cost = ([tcost.n, ocost.n] | max) + CARD_CHROME %}
{% set kv_tall_n = [tcost.n, ocost.n] | max %}
{% set kv_tall_lines = tcost.lines if tcost.n >= ocost.n else ocost.lines %}
{% set kv_tall_rows = (title_rows | length) if tcost.n >= ocost.n else (offer_rows | length) %}

{# --- the schedule of portions (multi portion properties only) ------------ #}
{% set portions = vm.portions or [] %}
{% set np = portions | length %}
{% set sched_units = np + (1 if np > 1 else 0) %}{# the total extent row #}
{% set sched_inline = (H3 + TH_ROW + sched_units * SROW + GAP) if np else 0 %}
{# Whole schedule beside the cards on page 2 (playbook 4.2), or nothing: half
   the rows on page 2 and the rest on a sheet of their own is what leaves a
   ragged tail. Past that it takes pages of its own, split evenly. #}
{% set sched_on_p2 = np > 0 and (sched_inline + cards_cost) <= REGION %}
{% set sched_own = np > 0 and not sched_on_p2 %}
{% set sched_cap = (REGION - TH_ROW - GAP) // SROW %}
{% set sched_np = ((sched_units + sched_cap - 1) // sched_cap) if sched_own else 0 %}
{% set sched_pages = portions | batch(((np + sched_np - 1) // sched_np) if sched_np else np) | list if sched_own else [] %}

{# --- the conditions of sale ---------------------------------------------- #}
{# The list can be model generated or human edited, so its height is measured
   (a term over about 95 characters wraps) rather than assumed. #}
{% set terms_all = vm.terms or [] %}
{% set term_lines = [] %}
{% for t in terms_all %}{% set _ = term_lines.append(1 + ((t | length) // TERM_CHARS)) %}{% endfor %}
{% set terms_cost = ((term_lines | sum) * LINE + (terms_all | length) * 2 * ROW_PAD) if terms_all else 0 %}
{% set p2_used = cards_cost + (sched_inline if sched_on_p2 else 0) %}
{# They stay on page 2 while they fit under the cards, which is the common
   single property case; only a genuinely full page 2 moves them off. Merely
   having portions is not a reason to give six short conditions a whole sheet. #}
{% set terms_on_p2 = terms_all and (p2_used + GAP + H3 + terms_cost) <= REGION %}
{% set terms_own = terms_all and not terms_on_p2 %}
{# What is left of page 2 once everything that belongs there is placed. On a
   data light record (no conditions, few deeds fields) that is most of the
   sheet, so the card rows are opened up to take it rather than leaving a third
   of an A4 blank under two short cards. #}
{# The threshold is high, and 15mm of the spare is left on the table, because
   the estimate is only good to about a centimetre: opening the rows up on a
   page that was merely comfortable would push it onto a second sheet. #}
{% set p2_spare = REGION - p2_used - ((GAP + H3 + terms_cost) if terms_on_p2 else 0) %}
{% set kv_fill = p2_spare > 400 %}
{# The two card and conditions paddings, resolved as numbers, so what is left
   after both have taken their share can be measured rather than guessed at.
   The conditions budget nets off what the cards took: they draw on the same
   spare height, and counting it twice would run the sheet long. #}
{# The card rows are opened up gently when a photograph band is there to take
   the rest of the sheet, and hard when there is no photograph on the record at
   all: an airy card is a poorer page than a tight one, but both beat a third of
   an A4 left blank under two short boxes. #}
{% set kv_cap = 50 if fill_photos else 115 %}
{% set kv_pad = (padraw(kv_tall_n + p2_spare - 150, kv_tall_lines, kv_tall_rows, kv_cap, KV_PAD) | int) if kv_fill else KV_PAD %}
{% set kv_extra = kv_tall_rows * 2 * (kv_pad - KV_PAD) %}
{% set p2_term_pad = (padraw(REGION - p2_used - GAP - H3 - kv_extra, term_lines | sum, terms_all | length, 80) | int) if terms_on_p2 else ROW_PAD %}
{% set p2_term_extra = ((terms_all | length) * 2 * (p2_term_pad - ROW_PAD)) if terms_on_p2 else 0 %}
{% set p2_left = p2_spare - kv_extra - p2_term_extra %}
{% set p2_band = fill_photos and p2_left >= FILL_MIN %}

{# =========================================================================
   LIST PAGINATION. Three lists can outgrow a sheet: the two feature columns
   and (on its own page) the conditions. Each is packed the same way, so the
   maths lives in one loop.
   ========================================================================= #}
{% set fm_all = vm.features_main or [] %}
{% set fc_all = vm.features_complex or [] %}
{% set feat_total = (fm_all | length) + (fc_all | length) %}
{# Short lists get one roomy full width column; long ones get two columns, and
   an item in a narrow column wraps at about 44 characters instead of 95. #}
{% set feat_stack = (not (fm_all and fc_all)) or feat_total <= 10 %}
{% set feat_chars = TERM_CHARS if feat_stack else COL_CHARS %}
{% set feat_shared = feat_stack and fm_all and fc_all %}

{% set fm_lines = [] %}
{% for f in fm_all %}{% set _ = fm_lines.append(1 + ((f | length) // feat_chars)) %}{% endfor %}
{% set fc_lines = [] %}
{% for f in fc_all %}{% set _ = fc_lines.append(1 + ((f | length) // feat_chars)) %}{% endfor %}
{% set fm_cost = (fm_lines | sum) * LINE + (fm_all | length) * 2 * ROW_PAD %}
{% set fc_cost = (fc_lines | sum) * LINE + (fc_all | length) * 2 * ROW_PAD %}

{# A feature page's first sheet also carries the stat strip and, where there is
   one, the flatlet callout, so it holds roughly 145mm of list against a
   continuation sheet's 200mm. Budgeting both at the same number is what turned
   38 features into three ragged pages instead of two full ones. When the two
   lists share one column they also share the sheet, split by weight. #}
{% set feat_ovh = (2 * H3 + GAP) if feat_shared else H3 %}
{% set feat_first = REGION_WIDE - (STAT_STRIP if stats else 0) - (FLATLET_BOX if vm.flatlet_present else 0) - feat_ovh %}
{% set feat_cont = REGION_WIDE - feat_ovh %}
{% set feat_den = (fm_cost + fc_cost) if feat_shared else 0 %}

{% set pack_items = [fm_all, fc_all, terms_all if terms_own else []] %}
{% set pack_lines = [fm_lines, fc_lines, term_lines if terms_own else []] %}
{% set pack_b1 = [
     (feat_first * fm_cost // feat_den) if feat_den else feat_first,
     (feat_first * fc_cost // feat_den) if feat_den else feat_first,
     REGION - OFFER_BOX - GAP] %}
{% set pack_b2 = [
     (feat_cont * fm_cost // feat_den) if feat_den else feat_cont,
     (feat_cont * fc_cost // feat_den) if feat_den else feat_cont,
     REGION] %}
{% set packed = [] %}
{% for items in pack_items %}
  {% set lines = pack_lines[loop.index0] %}
  {% set b1 = pack_b1[loop.index0] %}
  {% set b2 = pack_b2[loop.index0] %}
  {% set cost = (lines | sum) * LINE + (items | length) * 2 * ROW_PAD %}
  {# The tallest single row, held back on every page after the first so the
     last page cannot be handed more than it can hold. #}
  {% set mx = namespace(v=0) %}
  {% for l in lines %}{% if l * LINE + 2 * ROW_PAD > mx.v %}{% set mx.v = l * LINE + 2 * ROW_PAD %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  {% set nn = namespace(n=0) %}
  {% for k in range(1, 13) %}
    {% if not nn.n and cost <= b1 + (k - 1) * (b2 - mx.v) %}{% set nn.n = k %}{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% set n = nn.n or 12 %}
  {% set cap = b1 + (n - 1) * b2 %}
  {% set pk = namespace(out=[], cur=[], used=0, i=0) %}
  {% for f in items %}
    {% set c = lines[loop.index0] * LINE + 2 * ROW_PAD %}
    {# Each page takes the same fraction of its own budget as the list takes of
       the total, so no page ends up with the leftovers. #}
    {% set tgt = ((b1 if pk.i == 0 else b2) * cost // cap) if cap else 0 %}
    {% if pk.cur and pk.i < n - 1 and pk.used + c > tgt %}
      {% set pk.out = pk.out + [pk.cur] %}
      {% set pk.cur = [] %}
      {% set pk.used = 0 %}
      {% set pk.i = pk.i + 1 %}
    {% endif %}
    {% set pk.cur = pk.cur + [f] %}
    {% set pk.used = pk.used + c %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% if pk.cur %}{% set pk.out = pk.out + [pk.cur] %}{% endif %}
  {% set _ = packed.append(pk.out) %}
{% endfor %}
{% set fm_pages = packed[0] %}
{% set fc_pages = packed[1] %}
{% set term_pages = packed[2] %}
{# The flatlet callout rides the features page; it is not a page on its own. #}
{% set feature_pages = [fm_pages | length, fc_pages | length] | max %}

{% set any_portion_erf = portions | selectattr('erf') | list | length > 0 %}
{% set any_portion_deed = portions | selectattr('deed') | list | length > 0 %}

{# --- investment highlights: one row per real record fact ----------------- #}
{% set hl = [] %}
{% if is_auction %}
{% set _ = hl.append(('Offered on auction', ((vm.auction_type ~ ' auction, ') if vm.auction_type else 'Auction, ') ~ auction_line)) %}
{% else %}
{% set _ = hl.append(('How it is offered', offer_headline ~ ', subject to the conditions of sale')) %}
{% endif %}
{% if vm.location_line %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Location', vm.location_line)) %}{% endif %}
{% if accom %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Accommodation', accom | join(', '))) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.flatlet_present %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Separate flatlet', flatlet_line)) %}{% endif %}
{% if extent_str | trim %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Extent', (extent_str | trim) ~ (', being the total of the ' ~ np ~ ' portions listed' if np > 1 else '') ~ ', to be confirmed on due diligence')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.garages and vm.garages != '0' %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Parking', vm.garages ~ (' garage' if vm.garages == '1' else ' garages'))) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.title_type_label %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Title', vm.title_type_label ~ (', ' ~ vm.scheme if vm.scheme else '') ~ (' unit ' ~ vm.unit if vm.unit else '') ~ (', erf ' ~ vm.erf if vm.erf else ''))) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.zoning %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Zoning', vm.zoning ~ ', to be confirmed on due diligence')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.features_complex %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Complex and shared facilities', vm.features_complex[:4] | join(', '))) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.features_main %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Main residence', vm.features_main[:3] | join('; '))) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.viewing_by_appt %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Viewing', 'Strictly by appointment through Dynamic Auctioneers')) %}{% endif %}
{# A table of three or four rows is not a page. Below that the highlights page
   is dropped rather than padded out with invented selling points. #}
{% set show_highlights = (hl | length) >= 5 %}
{% set hl_lines = namespace(n=0) %}
{% for label, detail in hl %}{% set hl_lines.n = hl_lines.n + 1 + ((detail | length) // 69) %}{% endfor %}

{% macro running_head() %}
  <div class="rh">
    <span class="rh-b">{{ vm.brand_name }}</span>
    <span>{{ pack_label }}{% if vm.public_ref %} | Ref {{ vm.public_ref }}{% endif %}</span>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro page_foot() %}
  <div class="pf">
    <span>{{ vm.headline }}</span>
    <span class="num"></span>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro section_head(eyebrow, title) %}
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</div>
    <h2>{{ title }}</h2>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro stat_cells(cells) %}
  <div class="stats" style="grid-template-columns: repeat({{ cells | length }}, 1fr)">
    {% for value, label in cells %}
      <div><div class="stat-n">{{ value }}</div><div class="stat-l">{{ label }}</div></div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro kv_card(heading, rows) %}
  <div class="card">
    <h3>{{ heading }}</h3>
    <table class="kv">
      {% for label, value in rows %}
      <tr><td>{{ label }}</td><td>{{ value }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro schedule_table(rows, with_total, pad='') %}
  <table class="sched"{% if pad %} style="--srow: {{ pad }}"{% endif %}>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Portion</th>
        {% if any_portion_erf %}<th>Erf</th>{% endif %}
        <th>Extent</th>
        {% if any_portion_deed %}<th>Title deed</th>{% endif %}
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for p in rows %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ p.label or 'Portion ' ~ loop.index }}</td>
        {% if any_portion_erf %}<td>{{ p.erf or '' }}</td>{% endif %}
        <td>{% if p.size_display %}approx. {{ p.size_display }} m2{% endif %}</td>
        {% if any_portion_deed %}<td>{{ p.deed or '' }}</td>{% endif %}
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      {% if with_total and vm.size_display and np > 1 %}
      <tr class="tot">
        <td>Total extent</td>
        {% if any_portion_erf %}<td></td>{% endif %}
        <td>{{ extent_str | trim }}</td>
        {% if any_portion_deed %}<td></td>{% endif %}
      </tr>
      {% endif %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
{% endmacro %}

{# `heading` is optional on purpose: on a page whose section head already reads
   "Conditions of sale" a sub head saying it again is the same words twice. #}
{% macro tick_list(items, pad='', heading='') %}
  {% if heading %}<h3>{{ heading }}</h3>{% endif %}
  <ul class="ticks"{% if pad %} style="--tickpad: {{ pad }}"{% endif %}>
    {% for t in items %}<li>{{ t }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro hedge_note() %}
  <p class="note">
    All extents, figures and features stated in this pack are approximate. They are drawn
    from the deeds records, the property report and third party data, have not been
    independently verified, and are to be confirmed on due diligence. Amounts are in
    South African Rand.
  </p>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro offer_panel() %}
  <div class="offer">
    {% if is_auction %}
    <div class="lbl">Auction</div>
    <div class="big">{% if vm.auction_type %}{{ vm.auction_type }} auction{% else %}Auction{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="sub">{{ auction_line }}. Registration to bid closes before the auction.</div>
    {% else %}
    <div class="lbl">How it is offered</div>
    <div class="big">{{ offer_headline }}</div>
    <div class="sub">Written offers invited, subject to the conditions of sale and the seller's confirmation.</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{% endmacro %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ pack_label }} | {{ vm.headline }} | {{ vm.brand_name }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    /* Playbook 3, the LIGHT document palette (distinct from the dark ads). */
    --paper: #faf7f0;
    --paper-2: #f4efe4;
    --line: #e3dbc7;
    --ink: #211d15;
    --ink-2: #574f42;
    --ink-3: #8c8371;
    --gold: #9c7a24;
    --green: #465a30;
    --font: 'Montserrat', 'Avenir Next', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  /* The paper colour is set on <html> so it paints the whole print canvas: if a
     page ever does run long, the extra sheet is still ivory, not bare white. */
  html {
    background: var(--paper);
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact;
  }
  body {
    margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink-2);
    font-family: var(--font); font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; counter-reset: pg;
  }
  img { max-width: 100%; }

  /* One physical A4 sheet. min-height (not height) so a pathologically long
     value flows rather than being clipped away. */
  .page {
    position: relative; width: 210mm; min-height: 297mm;
    padding: 18mm 18mm 13mm; background: var(--paper);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    page-break-after: always; break-after: page; counter-increment: pg;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; break-after: auto; }
  /* Content sits at the top of the sheet and the hedging note (or, on the
     closing page, the registration block) is pinned to the foot, so a page with
     less data reads as designed white space rather than as a page that stopped. */
  .page__body { flex: 1 1 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .page__body > .note { margin-top: auto; }
  .page--last .legal { margin-top: auto; }
  /* A page carrying a photograph band gives the leftover height to the band
     instead of to these auto margins. Flexbox hands free space to auto margins
     BEFORE flex-grow, so leaving them on would starve the band flat. */
  .page__body--fill > .note, .page--last.page--fill .legal { margin-top: 0; }
  /* A record with no photographs cannot take a band, so the closing page (whose
     text is fixed and always runs about 50mm short) spreads its blocks over the
     sheet instead of stacking them at the top with the shortfall in one lump. */
  .page--last:not(.page--fill) .page__body { justify-content: space-between; }
  .page--last:not(.page--fill) .legal { margin-top: 0; }

  /* The band: photographs that take exactly the height a page has left over. */
  /* flex-basis 0 and minmax(0, 1fr) rows: the band asks for NO height of its
     own and takes only what the page has left, so it can never be the thing
     that pushes a sheet onto a second one. Without minmax(0, ...) a portrait
     photograph's intrinsic height becomes the row's minimum and the page runs
     long, which is exactly what happens with `1fr`. */
  .band {
    flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 0; margin-top: 7mm;
    display: grid; grid-auto-rows: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 5mm; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .band img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; min-height: 0; object-fit: cover;
    display: block; border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .rh {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 10mm;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 3mm; margin-bottom: 7mm;
    font-size: 8.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .rh .rh-b { color: var(--gold); }
  .pf {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 10mm;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 3mm; margin-top: 6mm;
    font-size: 8.5px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .pf span:first-child { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pf .num::after { content: counter(pg); }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 9.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .22em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold);
  }
  h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.14; color: var(--ink); }
  h1.h1--long { font-size: 24px; }
  h2 { margin: 2mm 0 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  h3 {
    margin: 0 0 3mm; font-size: 9.5px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .18em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .sec { margin-bottom: 6mm; }
  .sec::after { content: ''; display: block; width: 22mm; height: 3px; background: var(--gold); margin-top: 3mm; }

  /* Key/value card table, used by the title and offering cards. */
  .kv { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 11.5px; }
  .kv td { padding: var(--kvrow, 2.3mm) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  .kv tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .kv td:first-child { width: 40%; padding-right: 4mm; color: var(--ink-3); font-weight: 600; }
  .kv td:last-child { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }

  /* align-items:start so each card hugs its own rows: stretching a short card
     to match a long one leaves a large empty box on a data light record. */
  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 6mm; align-items: start; }
  .card { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 5mm 6mm; }

  .stats { display: grid; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .stats > div { padding: 4.5mm 2mm; text-align: center; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .stats > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .stat-n { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  .stat-l {
    margin-top: 1.5mm; font-size: 8.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .16em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  /* How it is offered: the auction line or the offers framing. Never a valuation. */
  .offer { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--gold); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 5mm 6mm; }
  .offer .lbl { font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); }
  .offer .big { margin-top: 1.5mm; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  .offer .sub { margin-top: 1.5mm; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-2); }

  /* Cover */
  .cover { padding-bottom: 0; }
  /* Everything above the dark contact strip. It flexes, so the strip is pinned
     to the foot of the sheet without an auto margin (which would eat the free
     space the hero wants). */
  .cover-body { flex: 1 1 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }
  .cover-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10mm; }
  .cover-logo img { height: 19mm; width: auto; display: block; }
  .cover-ref { text-align: right; }
  .cover-ref .ref { margin-top: 1.5mm; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); }
  /* The hero takes the cover's leftover height rather than leaving a band of
     empty paper above the contact strip: basis 100mm, grows to fill, capped so
     a small photograph is never blown up past what it can carry. */
  .cover-hero {
    margin: 9mm 0 8mm; flex: 1 1 100mm; min-height: 84mm; max-height: 134mm;
    overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .cover-hero img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .cover-hero--plain { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: var(--paper-2); }
  .cover-hero--plain img { height: 24mm; width: auto; object-fit: contain; }
  /* With no photograph and no stat cells the cover would run light, so the
     brand panel takes the space the stats would have used. */
  .cover-hero--tall { flex-basis: 128mm; max-height: 170mm; }
  .lede { margin: 3mm 0 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .cover .offer { margin-top: 7mm; }
  .cover .stats { margin-top: 7mm; }
  .cover-contact {
    margin: 0 -18mm; padding: 6mm 18mm; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper-2);
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 6mm;
    font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.7; letter-spacing: .02em;
  }
  .cover-contact .cc-web { color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; }
  .cover-contact .cc-r { text-align: right; }

  /* Schedule of portions (multi portion properties only). --srow opens the rows
     up on a sheet the schedule does not fill on its own. */
  .sched { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 11px; margin-bottom: 7mm; }
  .sched th {
    text-align: left; padding: 0 4mm 2.5mm 0; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
    font-size: 8.5px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .sched td {
    padding: var(--srow, 2.6mm) 4mm var(--srow, 2.6mm) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink); vertical-align: top;
  }
  .sched tr.tot td { border-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }

  /* Photographs. The rows share the height the page has left (grid-auto-rows:
     1fr on a grid that flexes), so four photographs fill the sheet exactly as
     six do and the page never ends halfway down. */
  .shots {
    flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 60mm; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    grid-auto-rows: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 5mm; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .shots img { width: 100%; height: 100%; min-height: 0; object-fit: cover; display: block; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .shots--1, .shots--2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .shots--3 img:last-child, .shots--5 img:last-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }

  /* Feature and conditions lists. --tickpad is computed per page so a short
     list fills its sheet instead of leaving a hole under the heading. */
  .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 7mm 8mm; }
  .two--one { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  ul.ticks { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  ul.ticks li {
    position: relative; padding: var(--tickpad, 2.5mm) 0 var(--tickpad, 2.5mm) 6mm;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink);
  }
  ul.ticks li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  ul.ticks li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: calc(var(--tickpad, 2.5mm) + 1.7mm);
    width: 2mm; height: 2mm; background: var(--gold);
  }
  .callout { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--green); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 5mm 6mm; }
  .callout .t { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  .callout .d { margin-top: 1.5mm; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-2); }

  /* Investment highlights: Highlight | Detail (playbook 4.5) */
  .hl { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 11.5px; }
  .hl th {
    text-align: left; padding: 0 0 2.5mm; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
    font-size: 8.5px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .hl th:first-child, .hl td:first-child { width: 34%; padding-right: 6mm; }
  .hl td { padding: var(--hlrow, 3.2mm) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .hl td:first-child { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }

  /* Steps, contact, disclaimers */
  ol.steps { list-style: none; counter-reset: s; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  ol.steps li {
    counter-increment: s; position: relative; padding: 0 0 4.5mm 11mm;
    font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink);
  }
  ol.steps li:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  ol.steps li + li { padding-top: 1.5mm; }
  ol.steps li::before {
    content: counter(s); position: absolute; left: 0; top: -0.5mm; width: 6.5mm; height: 6.5mm;
    border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
    font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  }
  .contact {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 8mm; align-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 6mm 7mm;
  }
  .contact-logo img { height: 20mm; width: auto; display: block; }
  .contact .who { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  .contact .rowline { margin-top: 1.6mm; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink); }
  .contact .rowline b { display: inline-block; width: 24mm; color: var(--ink-3); font-weight: 600; }
  .note { margin: 4mm 0 0; font-size: 10px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .disc p { margin: 0 0 3.5mm; font-size: 10px; line-height: 1.66; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .disc p b { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .legal { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 4mm; padding-top: 3.5mm; font-size: 8.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-3); }

  /* On screen (gate 2 preview, HTML fallback) the sheets sit on a ground so the
     pagination is visible; the printed PDF keeps the paper edge to edge. */
  @media screen {
    body { background: #e7e1d3; padding: 8mm 0; }
    .page { margin: 0 auto 8mm; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(33,29,21,.12), 0 10px 30px rgba(33,29,21,.14); }
  }
  @media print {
    .page { margin: 0; box-shadow: none; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="sheet doc">

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1 COVER #}
  <section class="page cover">
    <div class="cover-body">
    <div class="cover-top">
      <div class="cover-logo">{{ parts.brand_logo(vm, 'light', 'auctioneers') }}</div>
      <div class="cover-ref">
        <div class="eyebrow">{{ pack_label }}</div>
        {% if vm.public_ref %}<div class="ref">Ref {{ vm.public_ref }}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>

    {% if vm.hero_src %}
    <div class="cover-hero"><img src="{{ vm.hero_src }}" alt="{{ vm.headline }}"></div>
    {% else %}
    {# No photograph on the record yet: a composed ivory panel carrying the brand
       mark, never an empty grey box. #}
    <div class="cover-hero cover-hero--plain {{ 'cover-hero--tall' if not stats else '' }}">{{ parts.brand_logo(vm, 'light', 'auctioneers') }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    <h1 class="{{ 'h1--long' if vm.headline | length > 68 else '' }}">{{ vm.headline }}</h1>
    {% if vm.address or vm.location_line %}
    <p class="lede">{{ vm.address or vm.location_line }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {{ offer_panel() }}

    {% if stats %}{{ stat_cells(stats) }}{% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="cover-contact">
      <div class="cc-l">
        <div>{{ vm.brand_phone }}</div>
        <div class="cc-web">{{ vm.brand_web }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-r">
        <div>{{ vm.brand_email }}</div>
        {% if vm.brand_email_admin %}<div>{{ vm.brand_email_admin }}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# ------------------------------------------------- 2 PROPERTY INFORMATION #}
  <section class="page">
    {{ running_head() }}
    <div class="page__body{{ ' page__body--fill' if p2_band else '' }}">
      {{ section_head('The property', 'Property information') }}

      {% if sched_on_p2 %}
      <h3>Schedule of portions</h3>
      {{ schedule_table(portions, true) }}
      {% endif %}

      <div class="cards"{% if kv_fill %} style="--kvrow: {{ kv_pad / 10 }}mm"{% endif %}>
        {{ kv_card('Title and registration', title_rows) }}
        {{ kv_card('How it is offered', offer_rows) }}
      </div>

      {% if terms_on_p2 %}
      <div style="margin-top:7mm">
        {{ tick_list(terms_all, (p2_term_pad / 10) ~ 'mm', 'Conditions of sale') }}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if p2_band %}{{ fill_band(p2_left >= FILL_WIDE) }}{% endif %}

      {{ hedge_note() }}
    </div>
    {{ page_foot() }}
  </section>

  {# --------------------------------- 2b SCHEDULE OF PORTIONS (its own page) #}
  {# Only when the whole schedule cannot sit beside the cards on page 2. The
     rows are then opened up to fill the sheet, so a nine portion schedule is
     one composed page rather than five rows on page 2 and four on page 3. #}
  {% for chunk in sched_pages %}
  {% set slines = namespace(n=0) %}
  {% for p in chunk %}{% set slines.n = slines.n + 1 + (((p.label or '') | length) // SCHED_CHARS) %}{% endfor %}
  {% set srows = (chunk | length) + (1 if loop.last and np > 1 else 0) %}
  {% set s_lines = slines.n + srows - (chunk | length) %}
  {% set s_pad = padraw(REGION - TH_ROW - GAP, s_lines, srows, 100) | int %}
  {% set s_left = REGION - TH_ROW - GAP - s_lines * LINE - srows * 2 * s_pad %}
  {% set s_band = fill_photos and s_left >= FILL_MIN %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ running_head() }}
    <div class="page__body{{ ' page__body--fill' if s_band else '' }}">
      {{ section_head('The property', 'Schedule of portions' if loop.first else 'Schedule of portions continued') }}
      {{ schedule_table(chunk, loop.last, (s_pad / 10) ~ 'mm') }}
      {% if s_band %}{{ fill_band(s_left >= FILL_WIDE) }}{% endif %}
      {{ hedge_note() }}
    </div>
    {{ page_foot() }}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {# ------------------- 2c CONDITIONS OF SALE (moved off a crowded page 2) #}
  {% for chunk in term_pages %}
  {% set chunk_lines = namespace(n=0) %}
  {% for t in chunk %}{% set chunk_lines.n = chunk_lines.n + 1 + ((t | length) // TERM_CHARS) %}{% endfor %}
  {% set t_budget = REGION - (OFFER_BOX + GAP if loop.first else 0) %}
  {% set t_pad = padraw(t_budget, chunk_lines.n, chunk | length, 80) | int %}
  {% set t_left = t_budget - chunk_lines.n * LINE - (chunk | length) * 2 * t_pad %}
  {% set t_band = fill_photos and t_left >= FILL_MIN %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ running_head() }}
    <div class="page__body{{ ' page__body--fill' if t_band else '' }}">
      {{ section_head('The offering', 'Conditions of sale' if loop.first else 'Conditions of sale continued') }}
      {% if loop.first %}
      <div style="margin-bottom:7mm">{{ offer_panel() }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {# No sub head here: the section head above already says it. #}
      {{ tick_list(chunk, (t_pad / 10) ~ 'mm') }}
      {% if t_band %}{{ fill_band(t_left >= FILL_WIDE) }}{% endif %}
      {{ hedge_note() }}
    </div>
    {{ page_foot() }}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {# ------------------------------------------------------- 3 PHOTOGRAPHS #}
  {% if shots %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ running_head() }}
    {# --fill: the grid takes the height, so the footnote keeps its own margin
       instead of pushing the photographs up the sheet. #}
    <div class="page__body page__body--fill">
      {{ section_head('The property', 'Photographs') }}
      <div class="shots shots--{{ shots | length }}">
        {% for src in shots %}<img src="{{ src }}" alt="Property photograph">{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        Photographs are supplied for marketing purposes and are indicative of the property
        at the date of inspection. Fixtures, fittings and contents shown are not necessarily
        included in the sale and are to be confirmed on due diligence.
      </p>
    </div>
    {{ page_foot() }}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ------------------------------------------ 4 ACCOMMODATION AND FEATURES #}
  {% for i in range(feature_pages) %}
  {% set fm = fm_pages[i] if i < fm_pages | length else [] %}
  {% set fc = fc_pages[i] if i < fc_pages | length else [] %}
  {% set fml = namespace(n=0) %}
  {% for f in fm %}{% set fml.n = fml.n + 1 + ((f | length) // feat_chars) %}{% endfor %}
  {% set fcl = namespace(n=0) %}
  {% for f in fc %}{% set fcl.n = fcl.n + 1 + ((f | length) // feat_chars) %}{% endfor %}
  {% set fm_pad = padraw(pack_b1[0] if loop.first else pack_b2[0], fml.n, fm | length, 80) | int %}
  {% set fc_pad = padraw(pack_b1[1] if loop.first else pack_b2[1], fcl.n, fc | length, 80) | int %}
  {% set fm_used = fml.n * LINE + (fm | length) * 2 * fm_pad %}
  {% set fc_used = fcl.n * LINE + (fc | length) * 2 * fc_pad %}
  {# Stacked lists share the sheet top to bottom, so their heights add; side by
     side columns sit level, so the page is as tall as the taller one. #}
  {% set feat_left = (feat_first if loop.first else feat_cont)
       - ((fm_used + fc_used) if feat_shared else ([fm_used, fc_used] | max)) %}
  {% set feat_band = fill_photos and feat_left >= FILL_MIN %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ running_head() }}
    <div class="page__body{{ ' page__body--fill' if feat_band else '' }}">
      {{ section_head('The property', 'Accommodation and features' if loop.first else 'Accommodation and features continued') }}

      {% if loop.first and stats %}<div style="margin-bottom:7mm">{{ stat_cells(stats) }}</div>{% endif %}

      {# Two short columns leave a hole; one roomy column fills the sheet. #}
      <div class="two {{ 'two--one' if feat_stack or not (fm and fc) else '' }}">
        {% if fm %}
        <div>
          <h3>Main residence</h3>
          {{ tick_list(fm, (fm_pad / 10) ~ 'mm') }}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if fc %}
        <div>
          <h3>Complex and shared facilities</h3>
          {{ tick_list(fc, (fc_pad / 10) ~ 'mm') }}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {% if loop.first and vm.flatlet_present %}
      <div class="callout" style="margin-top:7mm">
        <div class="t">Separate flatlet</div>
        <div class="d">{{ flatlet_line }}. Accommodation is as inspected and is to be confirmed on due diligence.</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if feat_band %}{{ fill_band(feat_left >= FILL_WIDE) }}{% endif %}

      <p class="note">
        Accommodation is described as inspected. Room counts, sizes and finishes are
        approximate and to be confirmed on due diligence.
      </p>
    </div>
    {{ page_foot() }}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {# ------------------------------------- 5 INVESTMENT HIGHLIGHTS (2nd last) #}
  {% if show_highlights %}
  {% set hl_pad = padraw(REGION - TH_ROW, hl_lines.n, hl | length, 130) | int %}
  {% set hl_left = REGION - TH_ROW - hl_lines.n * LINE - (hl | length) * 2 * hl_pad %}
  {% set hl_band = fill_photos and hl_left >= FILL_MIN %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ running_head() }}
    <div class="page__body{{ ' page__body--fill' if hl_band else '' }}">
      {{ section_head('Why this property', 'Investment highlights') }}
      <table class="hl" style="--hlrow: {{ hl_pad / 10 }}mm">
        <thead><tr><th>Highlight</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for label, detail in hl %}
          <tr><td>{{ label }}</td><td>{{ detail }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {% if hl_band %}{{ fill_band(hl_left >= FILL_WIDE) }}{% endif %}
      <p class="note">
        Every point above is taken from the records held for this property. No market
        forecast, yield or return is stated or implied, and each point is to be confirmed
        on due diligence.
      </p>
    </div>
    {{ page_foot() }}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ------------------------------------------- 6 CONTACT AND DISCLAIMERS #}
  {# The closing page carries fixed text (four steps, the contact block, both
     verbatim disclaimers), which measures about 60mm short of the sheet on every
     property. So it always takes a band when the record holds a photograph: the
     one page whose hole does not depend on the data. #}
  <section class="page page--last{{ ' page--fill' if fill_photos else '' }}">
    {{ running_head() }}
    <div class="page__body">
      {% if is_auction %}
      {{ section_head('Next steps', 'How the auction works') }}
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Register to bid with Dynamic Auctioneers before the auction closes.</li>
        <li>The auction is held{% if vm.auction_channel %} {{ vm.auction_channel | lower }}{% endif %}{% if vm.auction_date %} on {{ vm.auction_date }}{% endif %}{% if vm.auction_time %} at {{ vm.auction_time }}{% endif %}.</li>
        <li>The highest bid is subject to the seller's confirmation.</li>
        <li>The successful bidder signs the conditions of sale and pays the required deposit.</li>
      </ol>
      {% else %}
      {{ section_head('Next steps', 'How to proceed') }}
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>View the property by appointment through Dynamic Auctioneers.</li>
        <li>Submit a written offer to Dynamic Auctioneers.</li>
        <li>Offers are presented to the seller for consideration.</li>
        <li>Any sale is subject to the conditions of sale and the seller's confirmation.</li>
      </ol>
      {% endif %}

      {{ fill_band(true) }}

      <div class="contact" style="margin-top:8mm">
        <div class="contact-logo">{{ parts.brand_logo(vm, 'light', 'auctioneers') }}</div>
        <div>
          <div class="who">{{ vm.brand_name }}</div>
          <div class="rowline"><b>Telephone</b>{{ vm.brand_phone }}</div>
          <div class="rowline"><b>Email</b>{{ vm.brand_email }}</div>
          {% if vm.brand_email_admin %}<div class="rowline"><b></b>{{ vm.brand_email_admin }}</div>{% endif %}
          <div class="rowline"><b>Website</b>{{ vm.brand_web }}</div>
          {% if vm.brand_address %}<div class="rowline"><b>Offices</b>{{ vm.brand_address }}</div>{% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="disc" style="margin-top:8mm">
        <h3>Disclaimers</h3>
        {# Both disclaimers are single unbroken lines on purpose: the playbook
           requires them VERBATIM, so the text must survive being copied out of
           the HTML source, not only read on the printed page. #}
        <p><b>Marketing note.</b> This pack is for marketing purposes only. It is not an offer, a warranty or advice. All figures are approximate and drawn from public deeds records, third party data and the owner's information, and have not been independently verified. Buyers must conduct their own due diligence. {{ 'Any sale by auction is' if is_auction else 'Any sale is' }} subject to the conditions of sale and confirmation by the seller.</p>
        <p><b>Legal disclaimer.</b> Whilst all reasonable care has been taken to provide accurate information, neither Dynamic Solutions 1068 (Pty) LTD Trading As Dynamic Auctioneers nor the Seller/s guarantee the correctness of the information provided herein and neither will be held liable for any direct or indirect damages or loss, of whatsoever nature, suffered by any person as a result of errors or omissions in the information provided, whether due to negligence or otherwise of Dynamic Solutions 1068 (Pty) LTD Trading As Dynamic Auctioneers or the Seller/s or any other person.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal">
        {{ vm.brand_reg }}<br>{{ vm.generated_note }}
      </div>
    </div>
    {{ page_foot() }}
  </section>

</div>
</body>
</html>
